3. Nex-N2-mini — Turbo Phase Twin — quantized derivative (this project's weights)
   Derivative work of Nex-N2-mini, redistributed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0 (attribution above preserved per Section 4(c/d)).
   Changes made to the original work (per Apache-2.0 Section 4(b)):
     - Converted from the original safetensors to the GGUF format.
     - MoE expert tensors quantized two ways and packed into one dual-variant
       ("twin") GGUF: a codebook-free 3-bit type (IQ3_A770, ~3.19 bpw) and Q4_K
       (~4.5 bpw); non-expert tensors quantized to Q6_K. Both quant sets use a
       llama.cpp importance matrix (imatrix).
     - The GGUF metadata `qwen35moe.block_count` and
       `qwen35moe.nextn_predict_layers` were set to 40 and 0 respectively so the
       model loads in llama.cpp. The MTP/NextN head is speculative-only and is
       absent from the published checkpoint; this is lossless for standard
       inference.
   The model weights are not otherwise altered beyond quantization.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Software, tooling, and data
----------------------------------------------------------------------

4. llama.cpp / ggml
   Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors and the llama.cpp contributors.
   Licensed under the MIT License.  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
   The included build patch (build/llama.cpp-turbo-phase-twin.patch) is a
   derivative work of llama.cpp's SYCL backend, type system, and model loader:
     - SYCL reordered MoE mul_mat_id decode + fused gate/up SwiGLU,
     - the GGML_TYPE_IQ3_A770 codebook-free 3-bit quant type (CPU + SYCL),
     - the multi-precision "tensor variant" model loader (the --sm twin swap).
   The original MIT copyright and permission notices are retained in the
   modified source files. Modifications by this project are likewise licensed
   under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

5. k-quants (Q-K block formats) by Iwan Kawrakow (ikawrakow) and the ggml
   authors, part of llama.cpp under the MIT License. IQ3_A770 reuses Q3_K's
   superblock bit-packing (2 low bits in `qs`, 1 high bit in `hmask`, 8×32
   sub-blocks with 4-bit scales); Q6_K is used for non-expert tensors.

6. Non-uniform code points. The IQ3_A770 8-entry value table is a NormalFloat-
   style (non-uniform, zero-centered) codebook, an approach popularized by
   QLoRA / NF4 (Dettmers et al., 2023, "QLoRA: Efficient Finetuning of
   Quantized LLMs"). The specific table and the codebook-free packing are this
   project's own; the design influence is acknowledged here.

7. Importance-matrix calibration: "calibration_datav3" by Bartowski, used to
   compute the imatrix that guides quantization. The imatrix is aggregate
   per-tensor statistics derived from the calibration text, not the text itself.

8. Evaluation: WikiText-2 (Merity et al., 2016; CC BY-SA 3.0) was used only to
   compute perplexity and KL-divergence. It is not redistributed in this project.

